 "finding": "EIGHT OPEN EDGES ARE NOW MEASURED REFUSALS INSTEAD OF UNASKED QUESTIONS, AND THEY DO NOT REFUSE ALIKE.  Every one of D-641's FOUR 3600 s TIMEOUTS is answered here in 3.0 to 27.9 router seconds.  TWO of the eight are LAND refusals that a corridor screen can never answer, because there is no corridor question until a land launches: `/SPI_B_SCK` at `U9.30` (`blocked by U9.31 x21, U9.29 x17, track x9, U9.33 x8`) and `/BQ25185_STAT1` at `U11.9` (`blocked by U11.10 x18, U11.7 x16, U11.6 x7, track x6`) -- both a package's own adjacent pins, the PM-3 signature D-640 measured on seven other lands.  The other six launch at both ends and die NO_PATH, and their escape counts say how much room the search actually had: `/I2C_SDA_INT` 71 -> 1 and `/SX1262_DIO1` 1 -> 10 are nearly single-threaded at one end, while `/BQ25185_STAT2` 25 -> 10 and `/WAKE_INT_N` 34 -> 7 are not.",
